<% content_for :title, "Data Grid — shadcnrb" %>

<div class="space-y-8">
  <div class="space-y-2">
    <%= sui.h1 "Data Grid" %>
    <%= sui.lead "A CSS grid with table semantics: columns that size like flex items, optional cards when narrow, a fixed header, pinned columns, cell selection and rows that stream in. For a plain semantic table, see Table." %>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "Installation" %>
    <%= install_block "data_grid" %>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "Usage" %>
    <%= sui.muted do %>
      Compose <%= sui.code "sui.data_grid do |g|" %> with <%= sui.code "g.header" %>, <%= sui.code "g.body" %>,
      <%= sui.code "g.row" %>, <%= sui.code "g.head" %>, <%= sui.code "g.cell" %>.
      Wrap in a <%= sui.code "card" %> for the bordered look, or leave plain.
    <% end %>

    <%= live_example frame: false do %>
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border">
        <%= sui.data_grid do |g| %>
          <%= g.header do %>
            <%= g.row do %>
              <%= g.head "Invoice" %>
              <%= g.head "Status" %>
              <%= g.head "Method" %>
              <%= g.head "Amount", align: :end %>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
          <%= g.body do %>
            <% [
              {id: "INV001", status: "Paid",    method: "Credit Card",    amount: "$250.00"},
              {id: "INV002", status: "Pending", method: "PayPal",         amount: "$150.00"},
              {id: "INV003", status: "Unpaid",  method: "Bank Transfer",  amount: "$350.00"}
            ].each do |inv| %>
              <%= g.row do %>
                <%= g.cell inv[:id], class: "font-medium" %>
                <%= g.cell do %>
                  <%= sui.badge inv[:status], variant: (inv[:status] == "Paid" ? :default : :secondary) %>
                <% end %>
                <%= g.cell inv[:method] %>
                <%= g.cell inv[:amount] %>
              <% end %>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "With caption and footer" %>

    <%= live_example frame: false do %>
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border">
        <%= sui.data_grid do |g| %>
          <%= g.caption "A list of your recent invoices." %>
          <%= g.header do %>
            <%= g.row do %>
              <%= g.head "Invoice" %>
              <%= g.head "Amount", align: :end %>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
          <%= g.body do %>
            <%= g.row { g.cell("INV001") + g.cell("$250.00") } %>
            <%= g.row { g.cell("INV002") + g.cell("$150.00") } %>
          <% end %>
          <%= g.footer do %>
            <%= g.row do %>
              <%= g.cell "Total" %>
              <%= g.cell "$400.00" %>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "Responsive, fixed header, lazy rows" %>
  <%= sui.muted do %>
    The table is a CSS grid with ARIA table roles. Column tracks come from the attributes
    on each <%= sui.code "g.head" %>: <%= sui.code "width: :fit" %> is
    <%= sui.code "max-content" %>, an Integer <%= sui.code "n" %> is
    <%= sui.code "minmax(min, nfr)" %> and shares the slack like a flex item, a String is a
    fixed length, <%= sui.code ":auto" %> (default) takes its content width. Flexible
    columns give up width first, down to <%= sui.code "min:" %>, so the scrollbar appears
    only once every column is at its floor. They truncate with a tooltip;
    <%= sui.code "wrap: true" %> wraps instead. <%= sui.code "align: :end" %> right-aligns,
    <%= sui.code "fixed: true" %> keeps a column in view while the rows scroll sideways —
    the first column pins at the start, any other at the end — and
    <%= sui.code "heading: false" %> keeps a heading screen-reader-only.
  <% end %>
  <%= sui.muted do %>
    <%= sui.code "cards: true" %> makes it respond to its own width: drag the corner of the
    dashed box. Below 36rem each row becomes a two-column card placed by <%= sui.code "card:" %> — <%= sui.code ":title" %>,
    <%= sui.code ":aside" %>, <%= sui.code ":footer" %>, <%= sui.code "false" %> to drop it,
    default a label / value line; a number instead of <%= sui.code "true" %> is the breakpoint in
    rem. Without it the grid stays a grid and scrolls sideways. <%= sui.code "g.header fixed: true" %> makes the body the
    scroll box, so both scrollbars sit on the rows, with the header kept in step by
    <%= sui.code "shadcnrb--data-grid--component" %>; give the box a height.
    <%= sui.code "selectable: true" %> makes it an ARIA grid: click a cell or tab in and use
    the arrow keys, Home / End within the row, Ctrl+Home / End for the corners; the selected
    cell is outlined and kept in view clear of the pinned columns.
    <%= sui.code "g.cell ..., selectable: false" %> keeps a cell out of it, as the action
    cells here. Rows keep coming as you scroll: the page renders the first page and a
    lazy Turbo Frame as the last child of the body, which fetches the next page once it scrolls
    into view; the stream replaces it with the page's rows and a fresh frame. A non-row child
    of the body spans every column, so no row or cell is needed around it. Those rows are
    rendered through <%= sui.code "sui.data_grid_proxy" %> with no column knowledge: each
    heading carries its column's cell classes and label as data, and the controller stamps
    them onto rows as they arrive.
  <% end %>

  <%= live_example frame: false do %>
    <div class="@container min-w-80 max-w-full resize-x overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-dashed p-3">
    <div class="h-80 @xl:overflow-hidden @xl:rounded-lg @xl:border">
      <%= sui.data_grid cards: true, selectable: true do |g| %>
        <%= g.header fixed: true do %>
          <%= g.row do %>
            <%= g.head "Order",    width: :fit, card: :title, fixed: true %>
            <%= g.head "Customer" %>
            <%= g.head "Notes",    width: 2, min: "12rem" %>
            <%= g.head "Ship to",  width: 1, min: "10rem" %>
            <%= g.head "Status",   width: :fit, card: :aside %>
            <%= g.head "Items",    width: :fit, align: :end %>
            <%= g.head "Total",    width: :fit, align: :end %>
            <%= g.head "Placed",   width: :fit, card: false %>
            <%= g.head "Actions",  width: :fit, card: :footer, heading: false, fixed: true %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
        <%= g.body id: "orders-body" do %>
          <%= render "demos/order_rows", g: g, orders: demo_orders(1) %>
          <%= render "demos/orders_loader", page: 2 %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%= sui.muted do %>
    The row partial both paths share, the loader, the stream, the action and route, and the
    demo data:
  <% end %>
  <%= source_block "app/views/demos/_order_rows.html.erb" %>
  <%= source_block "app/views/demos/more_orders.turbo_stream.erb" %>
  <%= source_block "app/views/demos/_orders_loader.html.erb" %>
  <%= source_block "app/controllers/demos_controller.rb", only: /  # Replaces the orders grid.*?  end\n/m %>
  <%= source_block "config/routes.rb", only: /^.*more_orders.*$/ %>
  <%= source_block "app/helpers/table_demo_helper.rb" %>
</div>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "Sizes" %>
    <%= sui.muted do %>
      <%= sui.code "size: :lg" %> relaxes row height and padding for index-style lists; data
      grids keep the dense default. The size is set as <%= sui.code "data-size" %> on the table
      and applied through descendant selectors, so <%= sui.code "g.head" %> and
      <%= sui.code "g.cell" %> stay size-agnostic.
    <% end %>

    <%= live_example frame: false do %>
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border">
        <%= sui.data_grid size: :lg do |g| %>
          <%= g.header do %>
            <%= g.row do %>
              <%= g.head "Name" %>
              <%= g.head "Role" %>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
          <%= g.body do %>
            <%= g.row { g.cell("Ada Lovelace", class: "font-medium") + g.cell("Engineer") } %>
            <%= g.row { g.cell("Grace Hopper", class: "font-medium") + g.cell("Admiral") } %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "API" %>
<%= api_table headers: %w[Method Renders Notes], rows: [
  ["<code>sui.data_grid</code>",                 "<code>div[role=table]</code>",   "A CSS grid. <code>cards: true</code> turns rows into cards below 36rem of the grid's own width, a number sets that breakpoint in rem. <code>columns:</code> (an array of column attribute hashes, or labels) renders the header itself, for tables built from data; each heading carries its column's cell classes and label as data; <code>selectable: true</code> makes it an ARIA grid with a keyboard-driven selected cell, dispatching <code>shadcnrb--data-grid--component:select</code>; <code>size:</code> is <code>:default</code> or <code>:lg</code>."],
  ["<code>sui.data_grid_proxy</code>",           "—",                              "Rows rendered outside a table block, e.g. a Turbo stream appending to the body. Takes no arguments: the controller stamps each cell from its heading when the row lands."],
  ["<code>g.header / body / footer</code>",  "<code>div[role=rowgroup]</code>", "<code>g.header fixed: true</code> makes the body the scroll box, kept in step by <code>shadcnrb--data-grid--component</code>; with <code>columns:</code> it needs no block. Footer gets a top border + muted bg. Header and footer are hidden in card mode. A non-row child of the body, a loader frame say, spans every column."],
  ["<code>g.row</code>",                     "<code>div[role=row]</code>",     "A subgrid of the table, or a two-column card. Hover highlight, supports <code>data-state=\"selected\"</code>."],
  ["<code>g.head</code>",                    "<code>div[role=columnheader]</code>", "Column attributes when no <code>columns:</code>: <code>width:</code> (<code>:auto</code>, <code>:fit</code>, Integer share, String length), <code>min:</code>, <code>max:</code>, <code>wrap:</code>, <code>align: :end</code>, <code>fixed: true</code> (first column at the start, any other at the end), <code>card: :title | :aside | :footer | false</code>, <code>order:</code>, <code>heading: false</code>."],
  ["<code>g.cell</code>",                    "<code>div[role=cell]</code>",    "First arg or block for content; <code>colspan:</code> Integer or <code>:all</code>; <code>selectable: false</code> keeps the cell out of the selection. Flexible columns truncate with a tooltip unless <code>wrap: true</code>."],
  ["<code>g.caption</code>",                 "<code>div[role=caption]</code>", "Renders below the table."],
] %>%>
  </div>
</div>
